w`\n**partition** the suite (`test_smoke_tier.py` guards it). The intent worth\ncorrecting: at 1378 tests the generous default has inverted the tier's\npurpose.\n\n## Approach\n\nTwo deliverables — the re-tier and the budget sensor. Measure first, then cut:\n\n- **(a) Measure.** One `-m smoke --durations=0` run (plus per-module wall\n  totals); record the module-level ranking in the close deliverable. Expected\n  shape: the cost concentrates in modules driving subprocesses / bootstrapped\n  scaffolds through `conftest.run_py` (subprocess-coverage overhead included) —\n  the same class the existing 15 SLOW_MODULES already name.\n- **(b) Re-tier to the budget.** Preferred: **keep the opt-out partition**\n  (new tests still default into the bar) but move whole modules to `slow` by\n  the measured ranking until smoke fits ≤ 60 s with headroom (~45 s target),\n  drawing the line at the mechanical boundary where possible (subprocess/\n  scaffold modules out; in-process unit modules in). Fallback if the budget\n  cannot hold that way: flip to the **opt-IN `@smoke` posture the kit itself\n  ships** (`project-trajectory/pytest.ini` uses opt-in marks with unmarked =\n  full-suite-only — the meta-repo would then match its own template; note the\n  erosion risk: new tests default OUT of the bar). Record whichever line is\n  drawn and why in the spec/close notes.\n- **(c) The budget item.** Declare the budget once and give it a sensor that\n  bites, in the repo's growth-sensor idiom (`test_module_size_ratchet.py`,\n  `test_dashboard_size_budget.py`):\n  - **Declared home:** a `smoke-budget` entry alongside the tier declaration\n    (docs/stack.ini `[tiers]` vicinity) — seconds for humans/CI, plus the\n    deterministic proxy below.\n  - **Deterministic sensor (always-on):** wall-clock asserts are\n    machine-dependent and flaky, so the *ratchet* budgets what is\n    deterministic — smoke-tier **membership** (collected-count ceiling, and/or\n    the SLOW_MODULES line itself). Exceeding it fails the suite with the\n    \"raise deliberately or re-tier\" message the size ratchets use.\n  - **Wall-clock check (where timing is stable):** CI times the smoke step\n    against the declared seconds budget (warn locally, enforce in CI — the\n    build session picks warn-vs-fail per lane and records it).\n- **(d) Update the declared surfaces** that state the bar's cost/shape:\n  status.md \"Bar (per commit)\" (~3.3 min text), the `pytest.ini` header\n  comment, `tests/conftest.py`'s WI-122 block, and the `session-protocol`\n  skill §3 if it names the runtime. `test_smoke_tier.py`'s partition guard\n  stays green throughout.\n\n**Hard edges:** no test is deleted or weakened — re-tiered only; the full\nsuite (`-q -n auto`, slice/phase close + CI) is untouched; `smoke`+`slow`\nremain a total partition.\n\n## Interfaces\n\nNo cross-module seam — acts only within `tests/` (conftest tiering, the new\nbudget sensor, `test_smoke_tier.py`), `pytest.ini`, and the declared-bar prose\nhomes (docs/status.md, docs/stack.ini comment vicinity, the session-protocol\nskill). Intra-module, test/harness layer. Nearest seam for reference: SR-007's\ndeclared stack profile (`docs/stack.ini [tiers]` is already the tier\ndeclaration check.py reads), unchanged in shape.\n\n## Done-when\n\n- [ ] Measured module ranking recorded; the re-tiered smoke runs **≤ 60 s**\n      wall at `-n auto` on the dev box (real output pasted; ~45 s target for\n      headroom).\n- [ ] `smoke`/`slow` still partition the suite (`test_smoke_tier.py` green);\n      no test deleted; full suite count unchanged.\n- [ ] The budget item exists: declared value + deterministic membership\n      ratchet that **bites** (mutating the tier past the ceiling fails), and\n      the CI wall-clock check wired with its warn/fail choice recorded.\n- [ ] Declared surfaces updated (status.md bar text, pytest.ini header,\n      conftest WI-122 block, session-protocol §3 if it names the runtime).\n- [ ] Commit bar green — run with the NEW tier (`pytest -q -n auto -m smoke`\n      + `check_docs.py`) plus one full-suite run proving nothing was lost.\n- [ ] Row set `done` (Deliverable filled, SpecRef cleared); spec archived to\n      `docs/archive/specs/` with close date.\n\n## Notes / open questions\n\n- Filed 2026-07-23 (owner directive: \"a smoke test is supposed to be just\n  that\"). **Re-fronted the same day (owner ruling): `Priority=1`** — the id\n  tie-break keeps WI-275 first, this WI second, so every subsequent session's\n  commit bar runs against the tightened tier.\n- The 79% smoke share means the bar currently *re-runs most of the full suite*\n  per commit — the cut is large by construction; expect smoke to land in the\n  low hundreds of tests. Anything cut still runs at slice/phase close + CI.\n- If the dev box's `-n auto` worker count materially differs from CI's, the\n  seconds budget is per-lane; the deterministic membership ratchet is the\n  shared floor — this is why the budget item is split in two.\n\n## Measured ranking & re-tier decision (WI-281 close)\n\n**Measurement (dev box, 2026-07-23, 3.11.9 venv, `-n auto`, 24 cores).** The\npre-change smoke tier: **1088/1378 tests, 351 s wall** (`5:51`; matches the\nspec's 6–8 min band). Per-module wall totals (setup+call+teardown summed across\nthe tier, `--durations=0`) rank the cost — and it concentrates exactly where the\nspec predicted, in the modules driving subprocesses/scaffolds through\n`conftest.run_py`:\n\n| module (moved to `slow`) | tier-wall s | module (moved to `slow`) | tier-wall s |\n|---|---:|---|---:|\n| test_gen_trajectory | 440.8 | test_modules_registry | 43.1 |\n| test_agent_loop_review | 179.5 | test_agent_loop_worker | 41.1 |\n| test_agent_loop | 170.5 | test_ac_advisory | 34.8 |\n| test_trace | 166.8 | test_check_stubs | 26.7 |\n| test_check_docs | 124.4 | test_perf_budgets | 25.2 |\n| test_registry_checks | 96.2 | test_procurement | 20.4 |\n| test_check_privacy | 87.4 | test_gen_release_checklist | 17.8 |\n| test_agent_loop_critique | 87.2 | test_assets | 16.5 |\n| test_check_harness | 79.3 | test_gen_arch_map | 13.0 |\n| test_trajectory | 60.5 | test_trace_golden | 12.6 |\n| test_components_registry | 58.4 | test_gate_policy | 11.2 |\n| test_derive_gate | 53.7 | test_run_menu | 11.0 |\n| test_gen_okf | 51.5 | test_agent_loop_env | 9.1 |\n| test_gen_trajectory_pending | 44.0 | | |\n\n**Line drawn — the MECHANICAL boundary (preferred approach, not the opt-IN\nfallback).** The opt-out partition is KEPT (a new in-process test still defaults\ninto the bar — the WI-122 \"never a false green by omission\" intent). The 27\nmodules above joined the 15 existing `SLOW_MODULES` (→ 42) on one rule:\n*cost dominated by driving the heavy scripts (gen_trajectory / trace / check\\* /\nagent_loop) or bootstrapping a scaffold as subprocesses → runs at close + CI, not\nper commit*. The retained smoke set is the in-process unit modules (decision /\nrouting / schedule / planning / registry-parse / dogfood-sync / the size &\nbudget ratchets). No test deleted or weakened; `smoke`+`slow` stay a total\npartition (`test_smoke_tier.py`); the full suite is untouched. The opt-IN\nfallback was **not** needed (the budget held with the opt-out posture intact).\n\n**Result:** re-tiered smoke = **360 tests → 7.29 s wall** (now 366 tests with the\n5 new budget/tier tests; still ~7 s), well under the 60 s bar and the ~45 s\nheadroom target.\n\n**Budget item (split in two, per the spec).**\n- *Declared home:* `docs/stack.ini [smoke-budget]` — `seconds = 60` (per-lane\n  wall target) + `max-tests = 450` (the deterministic proxy, ~23% headroom over\n  366 for in-process growth).\n- *Deterministic sensor (always-on, GATES):* `tests/test_smoke_budget.py`\n  independently collects `-m smoke` and asserts the count ≤ `max-tests`.\n  **Bite-proven live:** with the ceiling temporarily set to 300 the real count\n  (366) failed with the \"re-tier or re-stamp\" message; re-adding any one big\n  slowed module (test_agent_loop ~113, test_gen_trajectory ~98, test_trajectory\n  ~115) blows past 450.\n- *Wall-clock check (CI, WARNS):* `scripts/check_smoke_budget.py` times the\n  declared smoke command against `seconds`; wired into `.github/workflows/test.yml`\n  as a one-lane `smoke-budget` job. **Warn/fail choice = WARN**, recorded here:\n  GitHub-hosted runners have far fewer cores than the 24-core dev box the 60 s\n  target was set on, so a hard time-assert would be flaky — this follows the\n  repo's warn-first stance for noisy runtime metrics (perf budgets `Gate=warn`);\n  the deterministic ratchet is the enforced shared floor. A stable lane can pick\n  `--mode enforce`.\n\n**Deviations / carry-overs.**\n- **status.md bar text NOT updated here.** Done-when (d) lists `docs/status.md`\n  \"Bar (per commit)\" (`~3.3 min`), but the parallel-dispatch worker contract\n  bars editing root coordination truth (`docs/status.md`) on a train branch —\n  the integrator/owner must update that prose to the ≤ 60 s / ~7 s re-tier at\n  integration. The other declared surfaces WERE updated: `pytest.ini` header +\n  markers, `tests/conftest.py` WI-122 block, the `session-protocol` skill §3\n  (all three materialized copies kept byte-identical).\n- **One pre-existing Windows red remains in smoke:**\n  `test_session_stdin.py::test_run_session_codex_reads_last_message_not_transcript`\n  — a retained in-process module. This is **WI-275's** subject (the two known\n  Windows shim-refusal reds), not this WI's; it fails identically on the\n  integration base. Incidentally the *other* of the two\n  (`test_agent_loop.py::test_cmd_shim_cli_spawns_on_windows`) left the smoke bar\n  because its heavy module was re-tiered on cost grounds — so this change reduces\n  the smoke-bar Windows reds from 2 to 1. The Linux CI legs are green.\n","numLines":189,"startLine":1,"totalLines":189}}}
