{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdJg7SpDyLeAMgeBAu3UR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. The WI-281 implementation was already present as uncommitted work in the tree; I verified it end-to-end and committed it with the required trailers as commit `5defb52`.\n\n## What WI-281 delivers\n\n**The problem:** WI-122's opt-out smoke tier had inverted — 1088/1378 (79%) of tests ran on every commit at ~6 min wall, so the \"smoke\" bar was re-running most of the full suite.\n\n**The re-tier (kept opt-out):** 27 subprocess/scaffold-heavy modules joined the 15 heavy e2e modules in `conftest.SLOW_MODULES` (→42), drawn at the mechanical boundary (subprocess/scaffold-driven modules out; in-process units in). A new in-process test still defaults into the bar. No test deleted; `smoke`+`slow` stay a total partition.\n\n**The runtime as its own budget item (split in two):**\n- `docs/stack.ini [smoke-budget]`: `seconds = 60`, `max-tests = 450`\n- `tests/test_smoke_budget.py` — always-on deterministic membership ratchet (collects `-m smoke`, asserts ≤ ceiling)\n- `scripts/check_smoke_budget.py` + a warn-mode CI lane in `test.yml` — times the smoke wall vs declared seconds\n\n## Evidence I verified this session (Python 3.11.9, 24-core dev box)\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Re-tiered smoke | **366 tests / 7.02 s wall** — well under the 60 s bar |\n| Partition | smoke 366 + slow 1018 = **1384 = full** (exact) |\n| Full suite (nothing lost) | 1377 passed, 5 skipped, **2 failed** (6:43) |\n| Ratchet **bites** | ceiling→300 makes real count 366 fail with the re-tier message; restored to 450 → green |\n| ruff format + lint | clean |\n| `check_docs` | 0 broken |\n| Pre-commit floor | all steps PASS (skills-sync confirms all 3 skill copies byte-match) |\n\n**The 2 full-suite failures are the known pre-existing Windows batch-shim reds** (`test_cmd_shim_cli_spawns_on_windows` + `test_run_session_codex_reads_last_message_not_transcript`) — WI-275's subject, in files WI-281 didn't touch. This change actually *reduces* the smoke-bar Windows reds from 2 to 1 (the `test_agent_loop` one was re-tiered to slow). Linux CI legs are green.\n\n## Two small corrections I made\n- Fixed the close deliverable's \"5 new budget/tier tests\" → **6** (2 in `test_smoke_budget.py` + 4 in `test_check_smoke_budget.py`), matching the measured 360→366.\n\n## Deferred to the integrator (per the worker contract)\n- `docs/status.md` \"Bar (per commit)\" prose (`~3.3 min` → the ≤60 s / ~7 s re-tier), setting the work-items row `done`, and archiving the spec — all touch root coordination truth, which a train-branch worker must not edit. The spec's Deviations section records this.\n\nWorking tree is clean; the commit ends with the required `WI: / Train: / Base:` trailers."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":975,"cache_read_input_tokens":106125,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":975},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b3533dd0-fac8-43be-ba9d-3f05f7bc987b","uuid":"8d7f67b2-5157-4685-ba75-2f9759bb2a37","request_id":"req_011CdJg7RQeRJAwHLjHCmzqh"}
